WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.445 --> 00:00:02.457
- I always say chemistry is everything.

00:00:02.457 --> 00:00:04.252
Because if everything
went smoothly all the time

00:00:04.252 --> 00:00:05.318
we'd be very complacent

00:00:05.318 --> 00:00:06.873
and we'd stay in one place.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.467
One day at a time, one hour at a time,

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.092
don't get overwhelmed.

00:00:11.092 --> 00:00:12.830
You always hear that phrase

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.578
"hard work beats talent,
but talent don't work hard".

00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:17.360
Nobody knows what you can do but you.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.835
We work really hard.

00:00:18.835 --> 00:00:20.318
We have a great show.

00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:21.285
Let's just have fun.

00:00:21.285 --> 00:00:24.727
Create something of quality
that is really going to

00:00:24.727 --> 00:00:26.384
make a difference in the marketplace.

00:00:26.384 --> 00:00:28.461
We're all extraordinary.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.740
Nobody's the same.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.610
I cannot tell you how many people

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:32.872
tried to talk me out of that.

00:00:32.872 --> 00:00:34.351
Like please don't do this.

00:00:34.351 --> 00:00:35.796
You reach, reach way beyond way beyond

00:00:35.796 --> 00:00:36.863
and even if you fall,

00:00:36.863 --> 00:00:38.879
you still got so far.

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:41.259
She's an American actress, author,

00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:43.942
dancer, fashion designer, and singer.

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:45.259
She's the first Latina actress

00:00:45.259 --> 00:00:46.689
to earn over a million dollars

00:00:46.689 --> 00:00:48.468
for her roll in "Out of Sight".

00:00:48.468 --> 00:00:50.061
She's regarded as the most influential

00:00:50.061 --> 00:00:52.335
Hispanic artists in the United States.

00:00:52.335 --> 00:00:53.721
She's Jennifer Lopez

00:00:53.721 --> 00:00:56.257
and here are her top
ten rules for success.

00:00:56.257 --> 00:00:58.674
(swish bang)

00:00:59.778 --> 00:01:01.644
At the end of the day with an entrepreur

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:03.065
you're talkin about a creative visionary.

00:01:03.065 --> 00:01:04.391
You're talkin about
somebody whose the impetus,

00:01:04.391 --> 00:01:06.057
whose the spark...

00:01:06.057 --> 00:01:08.385
To the business, to everything.

00:01:08.385 --> 00:01:11.149
And then you're smart
enough to grab this person

00:01:11.149 --> 00:01:11.982
whose great at marketing,

00:01:11.982 --> 00:01:13.423
with this person whose great at

00:01:13.423 --> 00:01:16.851
all the different aspects
of what you'll need to make

00:01:16.851 --> 00:01:19.275
whatever it is your
business is to succeed.

00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:21.828
I always say chemistry is everything.

00:01:21.828 --> 00:01:24.488
You have to find chemistry with people

00:01:24.488 --> 00:01:27.244
and the people you have chemistry with

00:01:27.244 --> 00:01:28.195
doesn't always work.

00:01:28.195 --> 00:01:30.005
That first person that
you choose for that job

00:01:30.005 --> 00:01:32.686
is like "Uh, this not going to work".

00:01:32.686 --> 00:01:34.657
(laughing)

00:01:34.657 --> 00:01:36.334
But then there's the people that come in

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:38.971
and you just, you're like "Wow".

00:01:38.971 --> 00:01:41.373
Stuff happens when we're together.

00:01:41.373 --> 00:01:44.255
And I've been lucky enough
to have a lot of people

00:01:44.255 --> 00:01:45.088
like that in my life.

00:01:45.088 --> 00:01:47.516
And because I'm a Leo and I'm very loyal,

00:01:47.516 --> 00:01:48.582
I stay with those people

00:01:48.582 --> 00:01:50.482
and we're able to build
and build and build

00:01:50.482 --> 00:01:51.858
and think and create, and discover

00:01:51.858 --> 00:01:53.915
and keep challenging ourselves

00:01:53.915 --> 00:01:55.773
to be better and better and better.

00:01:55.773 --> 00:01:58.982
And what other produce could we create?

00:01:58.982 --> 00:02:01.018
What other thing can we do

00:02:01.018 --> 00:02:03.791
for the audience that's watching?

00:02:03.791 --> 00:02:08.351
Well, Luana, there's been
many mistakes I've made.

00:02:08.351 --> 00:02:12.597
I think that you only
learn, really, in this world

00:02:12.597 --> 00:02:16.853
from the mistakes you
make, from hard times,

00:02:16.853 --> 00:02:18.877
from going through difficult periods -

00:02:18.877 --> 00:02:20.165
that's when you grow.

00:02:20.165 --> 00:02:22.540
And we should look at these moments

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.379
as opportunities for growth

00:02:25.379 --> 00:02:27.892
and as almost blessings.

00:02:27.892 --> 00:02:30.231
Because if everything went
smoothly all the time,

00:02:30.231 --> 00:02:31.481
we'd be very complacent

00:02:31.481 --> 00:02:32.866
and we'd stay in one place.

00:02:32.866 --> 00:02:36.277
And we'd never, ever stretch ourselves

00:02:36.277 --> 00:02:37.613
or question ourselves

00:02:37.613 --> 00:02:40.934
or want to be better
people in a certain way.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:44.566
But these moments, they
force us to do these things.

00:02:44.566 --> 00:02:47.523
And those mistakes that I made,

00:02:47.523 --> 00:02:50.649
I can't just mention one mistake, I think

00:02:50.649 --> 00:02:53.781
of so many things that
through my life that I go

00:02:53.781 --> 00:02:55.747
"Uh, that one maybe was
not the right thing to do."

00:02:55.747 --> 00:02:57.302
But, if I hadn't of done that,

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:59.500
then I wouldn't have known it
wasn't the right thing to do.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.199
And so, those things are necessary.

00:03:03.199 --> 00:03:04.694
I love what I do.

00:03:04.694 --> 00:03:05.887
And I feel really blessed.

00:03:05.887 --> 00:03:07.104
And I always try to remember that.

00:03:07.104 --> 00:03:08.938
Because, like you said
when I walked in here,

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:10.275
You like "Ah, you have so much going on,

00:03:10.275 --> 00:03:11.199
so busy and everything",

00:03:11.199 --> 00:03:13.090
but the truth is like I told you,

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.479
what I'm doing downstairs with Kohl's

00:03:14.479 --> 00:03:16.262
is something I love doing.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.022
And that's my thing

00:03:18.022 --> 00:03:21.619
and it's like, how do I make this work?

00:03:21.619 --> 00:03:22.775
[Jennifer Lopez] How
do we figure that out?

00:03:22.775 --> 00:03:23.956
And how do I give my best to that

00:03:23.956 --> 00:03:25.296
and to everything I'm doing?

00:03:25.296 --> 00:03:27.018
And it's just one day at a time,

00:03:27.018 --> 00:03:29.041
one hour at a time.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:30.532
Don't get overwhelmed.

00:03:30.532 --> 00:03:31.981
It's not rocket science.

00:03:31.981 --> 00:03:33.203
I'm not curing cancer.

00:03:33.203 --> 00:03:34.714
I'm just entertaining.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.396
Hard work, I think, is
the most important thing.

00:03:37.396 --> 00:03:39.021
You always hear that phrase

00:03:39.021 --> 00:03:42.928
"hard work beats talent,
but talent don't work hard".

00:03:42.928 --> 00:03:43.761
It's good if you have both.

00:03:43.761 --> 00:03:45.143
(laughing)

00:03:45.143 --> 00:03:47.454
And I believe everybody does have talent.

00:03:47.454 --> 00:03:48.614
You got to find your talent and

00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:51.738
then you got to work really, really hard.

00:03:51.738 --> 00:03:53.494
And I just strive to be the best.

00:03:53.494 --> 00:03:55.532
And I think those are the
biggest key to success.

00:03:55.532 --> 00:03:58.315
But, the biggest one
of all is working hard.

00:03:58.315 --> 00:03:59.557
You can't accomplish anything

00:03:59.557 --> 00:04:01.978
if you're not in early and out the latest,

00:04:01.978 --> 00:04:04.331
which, I usually am.

00:04:04.331 --> 00:04:07.537
Nobody knows what you can do but you.

00:04:07.537 --> 00:04:08.512
Nobody can tell you.

00:04:08.512 --> 00:04:11.493
If I tell you all the people who
told me I wasn't going to act

00:04:11.493 --> 00:04:13.042
or sing, or dance,

00:04:13.042 --> 00:04:15.242
or I wasn't good at it,

00:04:15.242 --> 00:04:17.222
or that I should stop,

00:04:17.222 --> 00:04:20.797
or I should quit, or even
after I became famous,

00:04:20.797 --> 00:04:24.363
you know, for doing these things,

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:27.437
I would be locked in a house

00:04:27.437 --> 00:04:29.938
somewhere doing nothing.

00:04:29.938 --> 00:04:33.243
The truth is nobody
knows what inside of you.

00:04:33.243 --> 00:04:35.620
Only you know what's inside of you.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:38.125
Only you know what you can accomplish

00:04:38.125 --> 00:04:39.243
and what you're capable of

00:04:39.243 --> 00:04:40.832
and what your gut and your dreams

00:04:40.832 --> 00:04:42.603
and your desires, and your wants,

00:04:42.603 --> 00:04:43.554
and your ability.

00:04:43.554 --> 00:04:45.178
You only know.

00:04:45.178 --> 00:04:46.354
Nobody else knows.

00:04:46.354 --> 00:04:49.446
So, whatever you feel in
your heart and your gut,

00:04:49.446 --> 00:04:51.170
you should follow that.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:52.587
Follow that.

00:04:52.587 --> 00:04:54.435
And then if that changes one day,

00:04:54.435 --> 00:04:55.460
that's fine, too.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:56.404
And then, you follow that.

00:04:56.404 --> 00:04:58.193
But you're the only one who knows.

00:04:58.193 --> 00:04:59.468
Nobody else.

00:04:59.468 --> 00:05:00.301
[Interviewer] In Montreal,

00:05:00.301 --> 00:05:01.134
- Yes.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.012
[Interviewer] minutes before

00:05:03.012 --> 00:05:04.768
you're offstage ready to go on,

00:05:04.768 --> 00:05:05.985
[Jennifer Lopez] Yeah.

00:05:05.985 --> 00:05:08.169
- Where's that energy level,
what's going through your mind?

00:05:08.169 --> 00:05:10.841
- Oh, wow. Tons of adrenaline,

00:05:10.841 --> 00:05:12.448
but, it's funny right before a show,

00:05:12.448 --> 00:05:16.309
in the hours before a
show, you know it's coming.

00:05:16.309 --> 00:05:19.172
That hour before, you get that adrenaline

00:05:19.172 --> 00:05:20.740
and you get ready to go.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.279
But, for me, in the
minutes, in the seconds

00:05:23.279 --> 00:05:24.769
before the show starts,

00:05:24.769 --> 00:05:26.602
I get very, very calm.

00:05:27.497 --> 00:05:29.953
It's like everything goes whoooosh.

00:05:29.953 --> 00:05:31.412
- But this is the first solo.

00:05:31.412 --> 00:05:32.381
This is ...

00:05:32.381 --> 00:05:34.083
- Yeah, but it's fun.

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:35.284
And, you know I have Enrique with me.

00:05:35.284 --> 00:05:37.222
I did the solo stuff in South American

00:05:37.222 --> 00:05:39.873
so, that first night in Panama,

00:05:39.873 --> 00:05:42.540
for me, was a bit nerve-racking.

00:05:43.648 --> 00:05:44.643
It was so funny.

00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:46.555
We taped our prayer backstage

00:05:46.555 --> 00:05:49.877
and after the prayer, I was like,

00:05:49.877 --> 00:05:51.809
we work really hard.

00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:53.702
We have a great show.

00:05:53.702 --> 00:05:54.535
Let's just have fun.

00:05:54.535 --> 00:05:55.958
I had to remind myself.

00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:57.595
As much work as it is,

00:05:57.595 --> 00:05:59.061
and as much as I want to do well,

00:05:59.061 --> 00:06:02.040
and as much as everybody
there wants to do their best,

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.575
and be successful;

00:06:03.575 --> 00:06:05.880
At the end of the day, those
people are there to have fun.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.871
You have fun. They have fun.

00:06:07.871 --> 00:06:09.736
It's a successful night.

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:12.244
And so, that's what we do.

00:06:12.244 --> 00:06:15.477
- How do you stay, how
do you pick what is next?

00:06:15.477 --> 00:06:18.219
How do you just know that feeling where...

00:06:18.219 --> 00:06:20.838
- I think it is kind of a feeling.

00:06:20.838 --> 00:06:22.379
But it's also a

00:06:22.379 --> 00:06:23.354
dedication

00:06:23.354 --> 00:06:24.571
to creating

00:06:24.571 --> 00:06:26.904
one, a high quality product.

00:06:27.865 --> 00:06:29.893
Something that's authentic to you

00:06:29.893 --> 00:06:32.179
and your brand, which is I think,

00:06:32.179 --> 00:06:33.544
the most important thing.

00:06:33.544 --> 00:06:34.774
And something that is

00:06:34.774 --> 00:06:36.578
a differentiate of your product as well.

00:06:36.578 --> 00:06:38.486
Something that is only specific

00:06:38.486 --> 00:06:40.297
and not everybody else is doing it

00:06:40.297 --> 00:06:41.461
in the same way you're doing it.

00:06:41.461 --> 00:06:42.457
How do you differentiate

00:06:42.457 --> 00:06:45.728
that authentic product of high quality?

00:06:45.728 --> 00:06:46.882
Do you know what I mean?

00:06:46.882 --> 00:06:49.799
It's a combination of those things.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:55.101
And again, my team would
constantly challenging ourselves,

00:06:55.101 --> 00:06:59.268
whether it's movies, or brands,
or TV, or books, or music,

00:07:00.407 --> 00:07:04.694
or whatever it is to
create something of quality

00:07:04.694 --> 00:07:08.655
that is really going to make a
difference in the marketplace.

00:07:08.655 --> 00:07:12.364
When did I feel like I went
from ordinary to extraordinary?

00:07:12.364 --> 00:07:16.306
I have to tell you that I
always felt, from my parents,

00:07:16.306 --> 00:07:18.889
that you could achieve anything

00:07:20.154 --> 00:07:22.220
so long as you worked hard.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.637
They were all about hard work

00:07:25.503 --> 00:07:29.039
and being able to accomplish
whatever it is that you

00:07:29.039 --> 00:07:30.158
wanted to accomplish.

00:07:30.158 --> 00:07:34.325
That was the idea that was
put in my head very young.

00:07:38.111 --> 00:07:42.278
I like when they ask me what
would you want to be up there

00:07:43.519 --> 00:07:45.537
and they gave me a
choice of all these words

00:07:45.537 --> 00:07:47.011
and I said be extraordinary,

00:07:47.011 --> 00:07:50.167
because, I feel like
we're all extraordinary.

00:07:50.167 --> 00:07:51.623
Nobody's the same.

00:07:51.623 --> 00:07:54.053
There's no two people that are alike.

00:07:54.053 --> 00:07:56.920
And honestly, we all have the capacity,

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.848
and we all have it in us,

00:07:58.848 --> 00:08:02.602
the ability to do whatever
it is that we want to do.

00:08:02.602 --> 00:08:03.755
And all we have to do is kind of

00:08:03.755 --> 00:08:07.338
just put our minds to
it and just work hard

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:10.690
and you can make anything happen.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.504
For me was never about
money and stuff like that.

00:08:12.504 --> 00:08:15.023
The last time I did something crazy.

00:08:15.023 --> 00:08:16.712
- [Interviewer] Was it going
to Idol to do that thing?

00:08:16.712 --> 00:08:18.817
- I thing that was a big, absolutely.

00:08:18.817 --> 00:08:20.905
I cannot tell you how many people

00:08:20.905 --> 00:08:22.191
tried to talk me out of that.

00:08:22.191 --> 00:08:23.896
Like "Please don't do this".

00:08:23.896 --> 00:08:26.848
"This is the worst move
you could ever make".

00:08:26.848 --> 00:08:27.903
And I was like, you know what?

00:08:27.903 --> 00:08:28.736
I don't think so.

00:08:28.736 --> 00:08:30.202
It feels right for my life right now.

00:08:30.202 --> 00:08:32.395
I had just had the babies.

00:08:32.395 --> 00:08:34.242
They were just startin to walk and talk

00:08:34.242 --> 00:08:37.742
and really become fully functional people.

00:08:40.772 --> 00:08:42.436
And I just thought, you know what?

00:08:42.436 --> 00:08:43.753
They need stability.

00:08:43.753 --> 00:08:45.140
We've been traveling around.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.463
At that time Marc, their dad,

00:08:47.463 --> 00:08:49.455
was touring a lot.

00:08:49.455 --> 00:08:50.718
And I was traveling,

00:08:50.718 --> 00:08:52.061
and it was just like, you know what?

00:08:52.061 --> 00:08:53.979
This is going to be a good thing for them,

00:08:53.979 --> 00:08:55.492
for me, I love the show, and

00:08:55.492 --> 00:08:59.042
I just basically said to everybody,

00:08:59.042 --> 00:09:00.441
I kind of overrode it.

00:09:00.441 --> 00:09:02.132
I have to say Benny
was kind of on my side.

00:09:02.132 --> 00:09:04.024
He was like, "What do you
feel like in your gut?

00:09:04.024 --> 00:09:06.339
"I feel like business-wise,
for these reasons,

00:09:06.339 --> 00:09:07.438
"it could be good.

00:09:07.438 --> 00:09:08.992
"But, you have to feel good about it."

00:09:08.992 --> 00:09:10.834
And I said I feel like it's
going to be a good thing.

00:09:10.834 --> 00:09:12.616
I feel like I have
something to contribute.

00:09:12.616 --> 00:09:13.497
I love music.

00:09:13.497 --> 00:09:14.808
I love talking about music.

00:09:14.808 --> 00:09:15.641
I love artists.

00:09:15.641 --> 00:09:17.158
That's what I want.

00:09:17.158 --> 00:09:19.138
I think this could be a really nice thing.

00:09:19.138 --> 00:09:21.682
By the way, we only
signed off for one year.

00:09:21.682 --> 00:09:24.064
You know, it wasn't like
a thing where I thought,

00:09:24.064 --> 00:09:25.210
Oh God, I'm going to be here forever.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.472
I said no, I'll do it for a year

00:09:26.472 --> 00:09:27.483
and we'll see what happens.

00:09:27.483 --> 00:09:28.569
I wound up loving it so much

00:09:28.569 --> 00:09:29.976
that I did it for two years.

00:09:29.976 --> 00:09:32.449
And they asked me back, I was like okay.

00:09:32.449 --> 00:09:36.984
Taking risks, for me, has
been a big part of my journey.

00:09:36.984 --> 00:09:39.484
Just thinking outside the box,

00:09:41.733 --> 00:09:43.060
doing the thing that

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.321
everybody thinks is dangerous sometimes,

00:09:45.321 --> 00:09:48.028
and just knowing that you can do it,

00:09:48.028 --> 00:09:51.120
knowing that you'll get through it.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.368
Thinking big.

00:09:52.368 --> 00:09:56.110
It's something I say a lot
of times when I feel bored.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:58.723
I always encourage my fans to think big.

00:09:58.723 --> 00:10:01.146
Think as big as you can.

00:10:01.146 --> 00:10:02.442
You reach, reach way beyond

00:10:02.442 --> 00:10:03.519
and even if you fall,

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:06.324
you've still gone so far.

00:10:06.324 --> 00:10:10.381
Short on your goal, you
still have went so high.

00:10:10.381 --> 00:10:11.547
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:10:11.547 --> 00:10:13.244
I'd love to know which of J-Lo's

00:10:13.244 --> 00:10:14.964
top ten rules meant the most to you,

00:10:14.964 --> 00:10:16.605
had the biggest impact.

